findings.body:
`validateStoredKeyConversion()` is defined as a `static` helper but never called. With the project's `-Wall` flags (see `src/Makefile`), an unused static function triggers `-Wunused-function`. It also suggests an assertion was planned and then dropped. The helper also has an odd contract: when `keyFromStoredKey` is set, it only checks for non-NULL, so it would not catch a bad conversion anyway.

::code{file="src/dict.c" lines="101-109"}

Delete it, or wire it into a `debugAssert` if a real check is wanted.

Several hunks only reformat code and have nothing to do with the stored-key API. Examples include `dictGenHashFunction` argument spacing, trailing spaces removed in `dictSetKeyAtLink`, a trailing comment space in `defrag.c`, and a new trailing-whitespace line in `dictFindLinkForInsert`.

The noise makes it harder to review the real change, and it will show up in blame for these lines. Keep the functional diff separate from formatting. Some of the new lines still carry trailing whitespace, so the reformatting is also incomplete.

::code{file="src/dict.c" lines="1767-1772"}

The PR changes no tests. Existing coverage in `tests/unit/type/hash.tcl`, `tests/unit/type/hash-field-expire.tcl`, `tests/unit/keyspace.tcl`, `tests/unit/memefficiency.tcl`, and `tests/unit/moduleapi/hash.tcl` exercises the hash, HFE, and defrag paths end-to-end, so the refactor is not untested. But no test targets the new contract directly. There is no dict-level test that a dict with a non-identity `keyFromStoredKey` returns the right bucket for find, delete, add, and rehash. That is the exact gap the defrag bug above would slip through.

Add a focused unit test for a dict type with `keyFromStoredKey` set, covering add, find, delete, and rehash, and a defrag-style `dictFindLink` on a stored object.

